The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md, about 10 KB. It's on disk but not committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command you gave would have done nothing. I briefly force-added it, then undid that local commit, so HEAD is back at 7f0f3fcb and the working tree is clean.

What the planner should know:

• Build and runs: the harness verified the build at session start. My own run of yoyo -p answered PONG. The last 5 evolve runs succeeded, and there have been no reverts in 14 days.
• Two files that can revert a whole task:
  • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines and not in the size gate's list. Adding 14 more lines makes cargo test fail.
  • src/config.rs is 4851 lines against its recorded 4762. Adding 11 more lines makes it fail.
• Main new finding: OpenRouter users get guessed limits for non-Anthropic models. I ran google/gemini-3.6-flash and openai/gpt-6 through the built binary. Both print the guessed-limits warning: a 128K context window and replies capped at 4096 tokens.
  • The cause is in agent_builder.rs around line 995. The OpenRouter branch only maps anthropic/… ids, using yoyo's own hand-written lookup.
  • yoagent 0.26.7 (we're on 0.26.8) already has ModelConfig::preset("openrouter", …) for six vendors. Using it removes a hand-written copy, which is what @yuanhao asks for in #1122.
  • Caveats are in the file: yoagent's version has no prices, accepts only dotted ids like claude-sonnet-4.6, and has no gpt-6 entry, so some warnings will remain.
• The other candidates:
  • #1137: commands that write a file (goal set, init) exit 0 when the write fails. Claude Code 2.1.318 fixed the same problem in its logout and MCP commands.
  • #1136: subcommands still read a stray --word as input (goal set --bogus saves "--bogus"). This is the third ticket in a row filed as leftover from the one before. My Day 246 and 249 lessons say to fix every subcommand at once, working from the code's existing subcommand lists, not one command at a time.
  • #1135: yoyo map decides "(using ast-grep)" before scanning, so the label can be wrong when ast-grep fails and the symbols come from regex.
• Waiting on @yuanhao: #991 item 3 (keep or drop stream-json's collected_text). The either/or I posted on Oct 29 has no reply yet, so it stays on hold.

Two things that looked like bugs turned out not to be:
• With a bogus key, the 401 says "Missing Authentication header". curl gets the same text from OpenRouter, so yoyo is sending the header.
• A malformed .yoyo.toml already stops -p with exit 2 and names the bad line.

I saved one research note to yopedia, mapping recent Claude Code and Codex changes onto yoyo. Recall was by keyword search only, because the query endpoint said sign-in is required.
